{"name":"California Lilac","hex":"#bbc5e2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lilac","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large shrub of the genus Syringa, especially Syringa vulgaris, bearing white, pale-pink, or purple flowers.","A flower of the lilac shrub."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a pale purple colour.","Of a cat or its fur: having a pale brown colour, lighter than chocolate."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lilac"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ceanothus","blocks":[{"text":"Ceanothus is a genus of about 50–60 species of nitrogen-fixing shrubs and small trees in the buckthorn family (Rhamnaceae). Common names for members of this genus are buckbrush, California lilac, soap bush, or just ceanothus. The genus is native to North America, ranging from Canada and the United States south through Mexico to Panama, with the center of diversity in the California floristic province of the western United States and Mexico, where around ~42 species are endemic out of the roughly ~58 species in the genus. Most Ceanothus are shrubs, with some species rarely tree-like while others have a short mat-like habit. Species of Ceanothus can be evergreen or deciduous, may have thorns, and also have a diverse number of petal colors ranging from cream to deep blue to pink. Some reproduce strictly from seed, while others can resprout from their roots after a fire."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Ceanothus_americanus.jpg/330px-Ceanothus_americanus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ceanothus"},{"title":"California","blocks":[{"text":"California is a state in the Western United States. It is bordered by Oregon to the north, the Mexican state of Baja California to the south, Nevada to the east, Arizona to the southeast, and the Pacific Ocean to the west. With a population of over 39 million across an area of 163,696 square miles (423,970 km2), it is the most populous U.S. state and the third largest by land area."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Flag_of_California.svg/330px-Flag_of_California.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/California"},{"title":"Syringa","blocks":[{"text":"Syringa is a genus of 12 currently recognized species of flowering woody plants in the olive family known colloquially as lilacs. They are native to woodland and scrub from southeastern Europe to eastern Asia, and widely and commonly cultivated in temperate areas elsewhere."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Stockholm-lilac.jpg/330px-Stockholm-lilac.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Syringa"},{"title":"Lilac (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Lilac is a light shade of purple or violet representing the average color of most lilac flowers. The colors of some lilac flowers may be equivalent to the colors shown below as pale lilac, rich lilac, or deep lilac. However, there are other lilac flowers that are colored red-violet."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Stockholm-lilac.jpg/330px-Stockholm-lilac.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lilac_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/210403_039_Fallbrook_-_Ceanothus_pendletonensis_Camp_Pendleton_California_Lilac.jpg/500px-210403_039_Fallbrook_-_Ceanothus_pendletonensis_Camp_Pendleton_California_Lilac.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/210403_039_Fallbrook_-_Ceanothus_pendletonensis_Camp_Pendleton_California_Lilac.jpg/1280px-210403_039_Fallbrook_-_Ceanothus_pendletonensis_Camp_Pendleton_California_Lilac.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/210403_039_Fallbrook_-_Ceanothus_pendletonensis_Camp_Pendleton_California_Lilac.jpg/500px-210403_039_Fallbrook_-_Ceanothus_pendletonensis_Camp_Pendleton_California_Lilac.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A210403_039_Fallbrook_-_Ceanothus_pendletonensis_Camp_Pendleton_California_Lilac.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Ceanothus_thyrs._008_php.jpg/500px-Ceanothus_thyrs._008_php.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Ceanothus_thyrs._008_php.jpg/1280px-Ceanothus_thyrs._008_php.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Ceanothus_thyrs._008_php.jpg/500px-Ceanothus_thyrs._008_php.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACeanothus_thyrs._008_php.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Ceanothus_sanguineus_4839.JPG/500px-Ceanothus_sanguineus_4839.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Ceanothus_sanguineus_4839.JPG/1280px-Ceanothus_sanguineus_4839.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Ceanothus_sanguineus_4839.JPG/500px-Ceanothus_sanguineus_4839.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACeanothus_sanguineus_4839.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Ceanothus_cuneatus.jp